## Source
Path A UX dry-run (0152), severity: **Medium**

## Context
`integration.md` presents the pre-commit hook installation (step 1) before the
`.gitignore` guidance ("Optional" section at the bottom). But the hook actively
blocks committing `tickets/erg` on feature branches — so the first time a user
tries to commit everything, the hook fires with an error about a policy they
haven't read yet.

The gitignore decision (commit the binary on main, ignore it on feature branches)
is a prerequisite for understanding what the hook does, not an optional afterthought.

## Fix
Move the gitignore/binary-commit policy note before the hook installation step,
or add a sentence to step 1: "The hook will prevent committing `tickets/erg` on
feature branches — see the `.gitignore` section below for the commit policy."

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A user reading integration.md top-to-bottom understands the binary commit
      policy before they encounter the hook blocking them
